WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.336 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:04.437
-Hey, everybody.
I'm going to try to keep things

00:00:04.437 --> 00:00:05.838
moving a little bit faster

00:00:05.838 --> 00:00:07.473
because our last two
have been over 20 minutes,

00:00:07.473 --> 00:00:10.176
which the last thing we want
is for our average of these

00:00:10.176 --> 00:00:12.712
to go for 20 minutes or we are
no longer Emmy-eligible.

00:00:12.712 --> 00:00:14.581
So if I'm talking
a little bit faster, that's why.

00:00:18.952 --> 00:00:20.920
[ Laughter ]

00:00:23.456 --> 00:00:28.327
Two weeks ago,
I said in "A Closer Look"

00:00:28.327 --> 00:00:33.232
you can microwave your testicles
and was told you can't

00:00:33.232 --> 00:00:35.868
because it doesn't work
with the door open.

00:00:35.868 --> 00:00:37.804
So I had to,
last week in "Corrections,"

00:00:37.804 --> 00:00:41.307
let everybody down,
say that wasn't possible.

00:00:41.307 --> 00:00:43.843
Then a few -- I guess you would
call them life hackers

00:00:43.843 --> 00:00:47.379
said if you
break off the little...

00:00:47.379 --> 00:00:49.349
plastic door catches
and you put them in,

00:00:49.349 --> 00:00:52.618
it'll trick the microwave
into thinking it's closed,

00:00:52.618 --> 00:00:54.520
so you'll be good to go.

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:55.788
The dream's alive.

00:00:55.788 --> 00:00:58.557
[ Laughter ]

00:00:58.557 --> 00:01:01.661
I did an impression...

00:01:01.661 --> 00:01:04.730
in yesterday's "Closer Look"
of Darth Vader saying,

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:09.168
"Soon the universe
will bow to the Empire."

00:01:09.168 --> 00:01:13.305
The Empire was not trying
to rule the whole universe,

00:01:13.305 --> 00:01:14.907
just the one galaxy.

00:01:14.907 --> 00:01:19.712
So...
apologies for making them...

00:01:19.712 --> 00:01:21.447
I guess, like,
seem power hungry.

00:01:21.447 --> 00:01:24.250
[ Laughter ]

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:25.451
In my defense,

00:01:25.451 --> 00:01:28.955
it's not like they mentioned
or stress the...

00:01:28.955 --> 00:01:31.057
galaxy part in "Star Wars."

00:01:32.492 --> 00:01:33.425
Whoa, what's that?

00:01:33.425 --> 00:01:36.095
Right away?
[ Laughter ]

00:01:36.095 --> 00:01:37.831
Like seventh word?

00:01:41.367 --> 00:01:44.304
So, I said yesterday that...

00:01:44.304 --> 00:01:47.073
I've been traveling by Zorb.

00:01:48.708 --> 00:01:51.343
But then we showed
this picture right here,

00:01:51.343 --> 00:01:54.747
and I was told
this is not a Zorb.

00:01:54.747 --> 00:01:58.184
This is --
This is just a water ball.

00:01:58.184 --> 00:02:00.653
A Zorb has
two layers of plastic.

00:02:00.653 --> 00:02:05.057
And this one burns
because we were this close

00:02:05.057 --> 00:02:07.093
to getting Zorb as a sponsor.

00:02:07.093 --> 00:02:08.261
[ Laughter ]

00:02:10.696 --> 00:02:13.365
This has been "A Closer Look."

00:02:13.365 --> 00:02:14.901
Politics got you down?

00:02:16.301 --> 00:02:19.706
Wish you could roll down a hill
in a giant plastic ball?

00:02:22.675 --> 00:02:24.644
Try Zorb.

00:02:27.413 --> 00:02:28.714
Hey, this is a correction
for you guys.

00:02:28.714 --> 00:02:32.017
Catch up on "Severance."

00:02:32.017 --> 00:02:34.353
It's our jam. We're going
to talk about it a lot.

00:02:34.353 --> 00:02:36.088
You won't regret it.
Great first season.

00:02:36.088 --> 00:02:37.690
Perfect finale.

00:02:39.992 --> 00:02:41.661
So, pterodactyls.

00:02:41.661 --> 00:02:43.695
I keep calling them dinosaurs.

00:02:43.695 --> 00:02:44.830
They're not dinosaurs.

00:02:44.830 --> 00:02:46.465
They're pterosaurs.

00:02:46.465 --> 00:02:48.601
But kindly...

00:02:48.601 --> 00:02:50.570
many jackals have said,
"This isn't on you.

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:54.607
This is on the dinosaur toy
industrial complex,

00:02:54.607 --> 00:02:58.511
which has long sort of
thrown pterodactyls in the mix."

00:02:58.511 --> 00:03:01.013
Museum gift shops,
also to blame.

00:03:01.013 --> 00:03:02.948
And so kids are growing up
thinking pterodactyls

00:03:02.948 --> 00:03:04.384
are dinosaurs
when they're not.

00:03:04.384 --> 00:03:06.952
And that obviously was something
that I want to set out to fix,

00:03:06.952 --> 00:03:09.188
so I have taken it
upon myself.

00:03:09.188 --> 00:03:11.890
I've been going to parks,
playgrounds.

00:03:11.890 --> 00:03:13.092
You know, if I see
a group of kids,

00:03:13.092 --> 00:03:15.228
I walk over
and I tell them,

00:03:15.228 --> 00:03:18.798
"You're being lied to about
pterodactyls being dinosaurs."

00:03:18.798 --> 00:03:21.367
And the upshot of this is,
one, kids aren't listening,

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:22.935
and, two, I'm...

00:03:22.935 --> 00:03:24.904
I'm not allowed to go
in the park anymore.

00:03:24.904 --> 00:03:26.406
[ Laughter ]

00:03:29.675 --> 00:03:31.510
Few weeks back,
a lifeguard reached out

00:03:31.510 --> 00:03:35.247
to talk about the proper way
to put on rubber gloves quickly.

00:03:35.247 --> 00:03:38.951
Then I said, "Hey, if I'm
ever -- if I ever need CPR,

00:03:38.951 --> 00:03:43.222
don't feel like you
got to put on gloves,

00:03:43.222 --> 00:03:45.758
you know, for me."

00:03:45.758 --> 00:03:48.627
Shame on me.
They put on gloves for them.

00:03:48.627 --> 00:03:50.163
The lifeguard, you know,

00:03:50.163 --> 00:03:51.964
because, you know,
they don't want to catch dis--

00:03:51.964 --> 00:03:53.799
They don't want to do CPR

00:03:53.799 --> 00:03:56.535
on someone who might have
something they could catch,

00:03:56.535 --> 00:03:57.803
which that makes perfect sense.

00:03:57.803 --> 00:04:00.106
I was, you know --
I was being selfish.

00:04:00.106 --> 00:04:03.575
Just because you can't swim,
doesn't mean you also...

00:04:03.575 --> 00:04:06.179
can't have hepatitis.

00:04:10.717 --> 00:04:14.653
Last week's "Correction"
dropped on Earth Day,

00:04:14.653 --> 00:04:18.957
and...
a number of you said, "Hey,

00:04:18.957 --> 00:04:22.160
you were drinking water
out of a tiny plastic bottle

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:24.764
and if there's anything
we can do to help the Earth,

00:04:24.764 --> 00:04:28.634
it is to, you know --
you got mugs on your desk.

00:04:28.634 --> 00:04:30.803
Don't use -- We got to use
less plastic."

00:04:30.803 --> 00:04:32.037
I totally agree.

00:04:32.037 --> 00:04:33.973
I'm very excited to say
that I will be now --

00:04:33.973 --> 00:04:36.575
From now on,
I will be drinking out of this.

00:04:36.575 --> 00:04:37.977
And I think that's good
for the Earth.

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:42.148
[ Sighs ]

00:04:43.583 --> 00:04:44.851
[ Laughter ]

00:04:46.853 --> 00:04:48.021
[ Whispering ] I'm so sorry.

00:04:50.689 --> 00:04:53.059
This is the last time.

00:04:53.059 --> 00:04:54.727
[ Laughter ]

00:04:59.232 --> 00:05:01.701
[ Laughter ]

00:05:06.171 --> 00:05:07.340
Mmm.

00:05:11.076 --> 00:05:13.646
I was told my Vin Diesel
sounds like Sylvester Stallone.

00:05:13.646 --> 00:05:15.882
That might be a note
for Vin Diesel.

00:05:15.882 --> 00:05:19.852
[ Laughter ]

00:05:19.852 --> 00:05:23.122
I did a Michael Caine
impression.

00:05:23.122 --> 00:05:26.792
Not all of you were --
I'd say the reviews were mixed.

00:05:26.792 --> 00:05:29.929
But, you guys,
let's not forget...

00:05:29.929 --> 00:05:34.400
I played Michael Caine on "SNL."

00:05:35.734 --> 00:05:38.070
Yeah.
Pretty -- Pretty big for me.

00:05:38.070 --> 00:05:40.339
I don't -- Very hurtful

00:05:40.339 --> 00:05:42.508
how much they're splashing
that "vintage" on there.

00:05:42.508 --> 00:05:44.811
[ Laughter ]

00:05:44.811 --> 00:05:47.713
Now, you might be thinking,
"God, I'm surprised Bill Hader

00:05:47.713 --> 00:05:48.781
didn't
get to play Michael Caine."

00:05:48.781 --> 00:05:52.418
He wasn't there yet.

00:05:52.418 --> 00:05:55.354
There were still some crumbs
for the rest of us.

00:05:55.354 --> 00:05:58.057
This is -- This is some
pretty interesting history.

00:05:58.057 --> 00:05:59.158
Shoemaker, you remember this.

00:05:59.158 --> 00:06:02.829
You remember
what this aired after?

00:06:02.829 --> 00:06:05.364
This aired right after
Ashlee Simpson

00:06:05.364 --> 00:06:09.835
got caught lip synching,
which is why it wasn't...

00:06:09.835 --> 00:06:13.505
the buzziest thing
come Sunday.

00:06:13.505 --> 00:06:14.740
The great Jude Law.

00:06:14.740 --> 00:06:16.409
Jude Law was in my sketch,

00:06:16.409 --> 00:06:19.011
that is the -- I don't know
what you call it.

00:06:19.011 --> 00:06:22.982
Is it the the Holy Grail
of "Second Chance Theatres"?

00:06:22.982 --> 00:06:25.751
This would be my favorite one
if we could ever do it.

00:06:25.751 --> 00:06:27.387
"Hair Heads."

00:06:29.489 --> 00:06:32.591
There's Jude Law.
There's Fred Armisen.

00:06:32.591 --> 00:06:36.528
There's two actors who will not
be named playing Hair Heads.

00:06:36.528 --> 00:06:38.464
Bobby Moynihan.

00:06:38.464 --> 00:06:40.466
Wally, you were there
for "Hair Heads."

00:06:40.466 --> 00:06:42.402
-Yeah.
-Do you remember how it played?

00:06:43.569 --> 00:06:46.071
To silence. To exactly that.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:46.071 --> 00:06:47.606
You guys all did
a great impression

00:06:47.606 --> 00:06:51.009
of the audience
for "Hair Heads."

00:06:51.009 --> 00:06:53.345
Mentioned Goofy this week.

00:06:53.345 --> 00:06:55.415
Referred to Goofy as a dog...

00:06:57.449 --> 00:07:01.354
...and a bunch of you said
he was a cow.

00:07:01.354 --> 00:07:03.622
Now, thankfully,
some saner jackals stepped in

00:07:03.622 --> 00:07:08.460
and pointed everyone
to a Snopes article

00:07:08.460 --> 00:07:09.762
that debunked this claim.

00:07:09.762 --> 00:07:12.198
I guess the cow rumor started
because Goofy

00:07:12.198 --> 00:07:16.202
at one point dated
Clarabelle, the cow.

00:07:16.202 --> 00:07:17.569
But people pointed out
that Clarabelle the cow,

00:07:17.569 --> 00:07:20.673
also dated Horace Horsecollar,
the horse.

00:07:20.673 --> 00:07:22.875
So there are two things
to take away from this.

00:07:22.875 --> 00:07:24.644
It is Goofy is indeed a dog,

00:07:24.644 --> 00:07:26.913
and Clarabelle
does not have a type.

00:07:26.913 --> 00:07:31.951
[ Laughter ]

00:07:33.352 --> 00:07:35.721
Speaking of goofy
love stories,

00:07:35.721 --> 00:07:38.390
I said that Rudy Giuliani's
first wife

00:07:38.390 --> 00:07:40.026
was his second cousin.

00:07:42.361 --> 00:07:45.130
That was an incorrect statement.

00:07:45.130 --> 00:07:46.866
It is an incorrect statement
to say

00:07:46.866 --> 00:07:50.402
that Rudy Giuliani's first wife
was his second cousin,

00:07:50.402 --> 00:07:53.005
because she still is
his second cousin.

00:07:54.173 --> 00:07:56.942
[ Laughter ]

00:07:56.942 --> 00:07:59.812
And that's the great thing
about...

00:07:59.812 --> 00:08:02.114
marrying a cousin.

00:08:02.114 --> 00:08:04.316
Because even after a divorce,
you still,

00:08:04.316 --> 00:08:05.751
you know,
you still have that connection.

00:08:05.751 --> 00:08:09.188
[ Laughter ]

00:08:09.188 --> 00:08:10.823
They can't take it away.

00:08:17.730 --> 00:08:21.434
[ Laughter ]

00:08:21.434 --> 00:08:23.268
[ Whispering ] I don't know
why they're smaller now.

00:08:23.268 --> 00:08:24.904
This is even worse.

00:08:24.904 --> 00:08:27.573
[ Laughter ]

00:08:31.076 --> 00:08:32.712
[ Clears throat ]

00:08:34.546 --> 00:08:36.649
[ Bottle clatters in distance ]

00:08:38.083 --> 00:08:40.185
Called Andy Samberg last week
to ask him

00:08:40.185 --> 00:08:43.822
if he would be interested
in taking Nic Cage's advice

00:08:43.822 --> 00:08:45.891
and hosting "SNL" as Nic Cage.

00:08:45.891 --> 00:08:47.225
He did not answer.

00:08:47.225 --> 00:08:49.094
I said he wasn't home,
and then a bunch of you said,

00:08:49.094 --> 00:08:51.330
"Well, you called him
on a landline."

00:08:51.330 --> 00:08:54.066
It's just a way to say
that he didn't answer.

00:08:56.334 --> 00:08:58.737
So I do want to call him.
The other thing is he texted.

00:08:58.737 --> 00:09:01.340
He had time to text and said,

00:09:01.340 --> 00:09:04.710
"Tell them I got 'The New York
Times' spelling bee.

00:09:04.710 --> 00:09:07.046
I got Queen Bee,"
which is when you get everything

00:09:07.046 --> 00:09:09.281
in "The New York Times" --
A lot of doubters out there

00:09:09.281 --> 00:09:13.252
that don't believe
that Andy would get them all.

00:09:13.252 --> 00:09:15.453
So, you know, again,
this is like --

00:09:15.453 --> 00:09:18.290
I think less than 50/50 chance
that he'll answer, but...

00:09:18.290 --> 00:09:22.094
[ Cellphone beeps ]
Unavailable.

00:09:22.094 --> 00:09:24.396
That's just how it goes, guys.

00:09:24.396 --> 00:09:26.832
But it's good for us
keeping it under 20.

00:09:26.832 --> 00:09:27.934
[ Clicks tongue ]

00:09:30.068 --> 00:09:35.441
I talked about how Sean Bean
dies in most of his movies.

00:09:35.441 --> 00:09:36.876
Somebody said it's closer
to a third

00:09:36.876 --> 00:09:40.512
or a quarter of his movies.

00:09:40.512 --> 00:09:43.749
But we are talking about
Sean Bean death scenes,

00:09:43.749 --> 00:09:45.550
and someone -- a jackal wrote

00:09:45.550 --> 00:09:48.487
something that made me
laugh out loud when I read it

00:09:48.487 --> 00:09:51.490
because it was so succinct
and to the point.

00:09:51.490 --> 00:09:55.494
They wrote, "I would love to
watch a Mr. Bean death scene."

00:09:58.064 --> 00:10:01.767
[ Laughter ]

00:10:01.767 --> 00:10:04.670
We made a joke implying
that wrestling was fake.

00:10:04.670 --> 00:10:06.037
We should have been clear.

00:10:06.037 --> 00:10:07.739
The stories are scripted.

00:10:07.739 --> 00:10:09.108
The stunts are real.

00:10:09.108 --> 00:10:13.545
So, when a wrestler in the ring
gets hit with a chair,

00:10:13.545 --> 00:10:16.448
they are, of course,
at risk of injury.

00:10:16.448 --> 00:10:20.018
I should not have made light of
that, especially since if I --

00:10:20.018 --> 00:10:22.455
if I were to be hit
by a chair, I would die.

00:10:25.824 --> 00:10:27.025
Oh, mug.

00:10:27.025 --> 00:10:28.427
We were talking
about how the mug is coming

00:10:28.427 --> 00:10:31.496
and how I went down
to the merch people at NBC,

00:10:31.496 --> 00:10:33.365
because sometimes
it's a little slow.

00:10:33.365 --> 00:10:35.200
I was like, "Guys,
we really need this jackal mug

00:10:35.200 --> 00:10:36.568
as quickly as possible."

00:10:36.568 --> 00:10:38.203
And they said, "Okay,
but if we rush it,

00:10:38.203 --> 00:10:39.437
we might get something wrong."

00:10:39.437 --> 00:10:40.705
And I'm like, "How hard
could it be? It's a mug."

00:10:40.705 --> 00:10:42.374
And they're like,
"Okay, we're just telling you."

00:10:42.374 --> 00:10:44.076
And I'm like,
"Look, we just really need it.

00:10:44.076 --> 00:10:46.612
The jackals have been so loyal.
Let's get them their mugs."

00:10:46.612 --> 00:10:48.180
And then they sent me
a prototype.

00:10:48.180 --> 00:10:50.416
And this...
This is what we got.

00:10:50.416 --> 00:10:55.053
[ Laughter ]

00:10:55.053 --> 00:10:58.223
I was like,
"How could you get that wrong?"

00:10:58.223 --> 00:11:00.358
And they were like, "We told --
We told..."

00:11:00.358 --> 00:11:01.961
And I was like,
"How do you even pick it up?"

00:11:03.728 --> 00:11:05.131
Because if it's hot...

00:11:06.698 --> 00:11:08.668
Anyway,
it's going to be a while.

00:11:11.336 --> 00:11:12.838
This -- Somebody did the math.

00:11:12.838 --> 00:11:15.640
If you add up all the
"Corrections" so far,

00:11:15.640 --> 00:11:20.479
10 hours, 17 minutes.

00:11:20.479 --> 00:11:24.750
"Lord of the Rings" --
9 hours, 17 minutes.

00:11:24.750 --> 00:11:27.652
Extended version
"Lord of the Rings" --

00:11:27.652 --> 00:11:29.388
11 hours, 22 minutes.

00:11:29.388 --> 00:11:32.191
Which is amazing.

00:11:32.191 --> 00:11:34.760
There's an extended version...

00:11:36.929 --> 00:11:41.167
...of "Lord of the Rings"
for -- for who?

00:11:41.167 --> 00:11:43.001
[ Chuckles ]

00:11:43.001 --> 00:11:45.437
Oh, you got-- Oh,
there's an extended

00:11:45.437 --> 00:11:47.873
march of the Ents.

00:11:47.873 --> 00:11:50.276
Do you like
slow-moving tree people?

00:11:52.044 --> 00:11:54.012
They really --
They really take their time

00:11:54.012 --> 00:11:56.649
pushing through the brush.

00:11:58.350 --> 00:12:00.086
Book update!

00:12:01.519 --> 00:12:03.289
You guys,
I talked about my book,

00:12:03.289 --> 00:12:04.423
"I'm Not Scared, You're Scared."

00:12:04.423 --> 00:12:05.324
There we go.

00:12:05.324 --> 00:12:06.558
And we had this helpful thing

00:12:06.558 --> 00:12:08.193
that was sent to us
by "The New York Times,"

00:12:08.193 --> 00:12:10.629
Week One, we were three.

00:12:10.629 --> 00:12:11.964
Then we were four,
then we were six,

00:12:11.964 --> 00:12:13.265
and then we were eight,
and we were nine.

00:12:13.265 --> 00:12:15.367
However, you might remember last
week during "Corrections"

00:12:15.367 --> 00:12:18.069
I said, "Hey guys,
a lot of Easter books up there.

00:12:18.069 --> 00:12:19.471
Easter is over.

00:12:19.471 --> 00:12:22.174
I think we got a chance
to stick around and..."

00:12:22.174 --> 00:12:24.276
Hold on one sec.
This is the big reveal.

00:12:27.979 --> 00:12:29.915
That's right. Sev--
We bounced up.

00:12:29.915 --> 00:12:35.054
Post-Easter bounce up to seven.

00:12:37.255 --> 00:12:40.793
My colleague Jimmy Fallon's
book right here,

00:12:40.793 --> 00:12:42.994
"Nana Loves You More,"
also got the bounce

00:12:42.994 --> 00:12:45.296
back up to two.

00:12:45.296 --> 00:12:47.332
So I do hope I catch him.

00:12:47.332 --> 00:12:50.269
And you will know
that I have caught Jimmy

00:12:50.269 --> 00:12:52.070
on "The New York Times'"
bestseller list...

00:12:52.070 --> 00:12:54.807
when I don't mention it.

00:12:54.807 --> 00:12:57.443
[ Laughter ]

00:12:59.811 --> 00:13:01.447
Respect the lead in.

00:13:05.951 --> 00:13:07.919
Um...

00:13:07.919 --> 00:13:09.421
Up.

00:13:09.421 --> 00:13:14.893
We were talking about
grammar in Eminem songs,

00:13:14.893 --> 00:13:18.898
and I warned jackals
not to criticize Eminem.

00:13:18.898 --> 00:13:20.466
And...

00:13:23.368 --> 00:13:25.304
...I said, "What's next?
You're going to say,

00:13:25.304 --> 00:13:27.706
'Will the please -- you know,

00:13:27.706 --> 00:13:30.943
will the real Slim Shady
please stand up?'

00:13:30.943 --> 00:13:33.846
What? Ending your sentences
with prepositions much?"

00:13:33.846 --> 00:13:36.714
And...

00:13:36.714 --> 00:13:38.116
Turns up, I got it wrong.

00:13:38.116 --> 00:13:40.886
"Up" in that case is an adverb.

00:13:40.886 --> 00:13:44.356
It's not a preposition.

00:13:44.356 --> 00:13:45.991
And that was...

00:13:53.032 --> 00:13:56.669
[ Laughter ]

00:14:00.305 --> 00:14:01.140
[ Clattering ]

00:14:01.140 --> 00:14:03.876
[ Laughter ]

00:14:06.111 --> 00:14:09.714
And it's really exciting.
I got a letter.

00:14:09.714 --> 00:14:13.819
The person -- One of the people
who responded was...

00:14:13.819 --> 00:14:16.822
Well...This is new.

00:14:16.822 --> 00:14:18.657
You can tell this is a new
letter that I just received

00:14:18.657 --> 00:14:20.659
because no --
there's no fire damage.

00:14:24.863 --> 00:14:26.498
Okay. So, there it says to me,

00:14:26.498 --> 00:14:30.302
and it says, "All these jackals
are jerks to be fanatical

00:14:30.302 --> 00:14:32.370
so let 'em know my lyrics
are perfectly grammatical.

00:14:32.370 --> 00:14:34.572
And you, you're the one
that got the adverb wrong,

00:14:34.572 --> 00:14:36.675
and I'm the one who found a curb
to stomp you on.

00:14:36.675 --> 00:14:38.477
Oh [bleep],
that "on" was a preposition,

00:14:38.477 --> 00:14:40.979
but let me address this mess in
a lesson if you'll listen.

00:14:40.979 --> 00:14:43.616
Wherever I put a word
is where it's gonna go.

00:14:43.616 --> 00:14:46.885
[Bleep] Strunk, [bleep] White.
That's all you gotta know."

00:14:46.885 --> 00:14:48.353
And then it's signed.

00:14:48.353 --> 00:14:49.721
You see where it's sighed?

00:14:49.721 --> 00:14:51.724
"Eminem. Be white."

00:14:56.161 --> 00:14:57.263
Pretty cool.

